From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: clear cached rate on station re-add

A full firmware recovery reuses the station's default link object.  Clear
its cached TX rate when the link is reinitialized.  This leaves the cache
unset, so the first legacy firmware placeholder remains ignored for an
HT-or-newer station until the firmware reports a valid post-reset rate.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1023,6 +1023,7 @@
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&msta_link->rc_list);
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&msta_link->wcid.poll_list);
+	memset(&msta_link->wcid.rate, 0, sizeof(msta_link->wcid.rate));
 	msta_link->sta = msta;
 	msta_link->wcid.sta = 1;
 	msta_link->wcid.idx = idx;
